# Codex refresh review: disk-substructure-profiles
VERDICT: FIX
REFRESH: PARTIAL

## Findings

- RR-01 | medium | broken-edit | “Built from 434 on-topic … 150 … off-topic” | The pack documents 584 papers; parameters.md supplies only 52 exclusions, so the claimed 434-paper screen is not reproducible. Its “left out of every count” also contradicts the software table’s all-584 denominator. | State the verified 584-paper provenance; complete and reconcile the exclusion list before asserting 434, and distinguish filtered counts from unfiltered aggregates.
- RR-02 | medium | stale | “Flux calibration … 5”; “2.3 in 6”; “20 K in 7” | These remain incomplete against visible new-pack entries. Calibration already exceeds five with 2020ApJ...891...48H, 2018A&A...616A..88V, 2021A&A...648A..33M, 2024A&A...689A.104D, 2024ApJ...974L..25D and 2025A&A...703A..15M. The pack also explicitly supplies κ=2.3 and T=20 K for 2024A&A...692A.155K and 2025ApJ...993...90S. | Recount distinct sources consistently across the rebuilt pack; label any retained subset tally with its actual coverage rather than implying a completed recount.
- RR-03 | low | attribution | “1–3 self-cal rounds set by S/N” | 2024PASJ...76..437Y step 3 specifies two total rounds below S/N 100 and three above it; it supplies no one-round branch. | Change to “2–3 rounds in this study,” distinguishing phase-only from amplitude-and-phase rounds.
- RR-04 | medium | attribution | “flaring angle 0.02 … 2024PASJ...76..437Y” | That paper’s step 13 explicitly uses 0.05 for DM Tau and GM Aur. The omission matters because the inferred temperature feeds the physical interpretation. | Preserve the two exceptions wherever summarising this study’s temperature prescription.
- RR-05 | medium | attribution | “Zhang … h/r 0.05” | 2024PASJ...76..437Y step 13 gives h_gap/r_gap=0.05–0.1 and restricts mass inference to gaps within the model range; only 11 qualify. | Separate the 2021ApJ...923..121Y example from other studies’ settings; require the local aspect ratio and a calibration-domain check.
- RR-06 | medium | attribution | “about 0.1 in the first ring” | 2025ApJ...989L..43Y reports **H/R ≥ 0.1**, with 0.15 and 0.2 producing similar results, rather than a measurement concentrated around 0.1. Its outer limit is explicitly approximate and sensitivity limited. | Retain the lower-bound direction and qualify the outer bound and model dependence.
- RR-07 | low | unsupported | “use [SpM] for azimuthal averages only” | 2024PASJ...76..437Y step 10 says averaging suppresses clump/speckle artefacts; it does not establish this exclusive restriction on SpM use. | Present averaging as the supported mitigation and label any stricter restriction as the skill author’s recommendation.
- RR-08 | medium | science | “D(r) = (1/I) dI/dr, inflections at D'' = 0” | The pack’s 2024PASJ...76..437Y step-11 summary repeats this criterion, but D''=0 concerns inflections of D, not ordinary intensity-profile inflections I''=0. The recipe conflates them. | Identify the paper-specific feature criterion explicitly; distinguish it from intensity inflections and specify what function Kneed receives.
- RR-09 | medium | science | “synthesized-beam convolution before comparing with the dirty image” | “Synthesized beam” leaves the response ambiguous. The explicit forward model in 2017MNRAS.469.3200B step 2 multiplies by the primary beam and convolves with the **dirty beam** before comparison with the dirty image. | Require the actual dirty PSF for dirty-image likelihoods; distinguish it from a restoring Gaussian.
- RR-10 | medium | omission | “frank … Fourier-Bessel fit to the real visibilities” | The recipe omits central stellar-source handling. Both 2020MNRAS.498.1319M step 3 and 2026A&A...705A.196H steps 2–3 explicitly subtract or otherwise specify stellar flux, including source-specific exceptions. | Add a prerequisite to model or subtract the centred stellar component, propagate its uncertainty and document exceptions.
- RR-11 | medium | omission | “Debris rings: peak radius, 25/50/75%-of-peak radii” | ARKS measures these on **surface-density profiles** after its step-6 temperature/opacity conversion, not indiscriminately on I(r). Its step 7 also defines the baseline as the adjacent gap minimum, otherwise zero. | Specify the profile quantity and measure fractions relative to the stated baseline; distinguish brightness metrics from density metrics.
- RR-12 | medium | omission | “eccentricity … from … the outer-edge slope” | This advertised use has no executable method. 2026A&A...705A.196H step 11 supplies e_rms≈0.77 l_out/R_out, Rayleigh-distribution assumptions, the R_out definition and restrictions to outermost rings/main halo belts. | Add the diagnostic and its restrictions, distinguishing particle RMS eccentricity from star–ring-offset eccentricity.
- RR-13 | medium | usability | “an edge-on version for inclined discs” | ARKS step 3 uses the edge-on rave version for three highly inclined discs **without a resolved central cavity**, tests both versions and selects the more appropriate result. Inclination alone is an incomplete routing rule. | State the actual selection criterion and require comparison of versions where applicability is uncertain.
- RR-14 | low | broken-edit | “Settings for 15 papers … named in references/parameters.md” | No identifiable list of those 15 inherited sources appears in the supplied reference. Their provenance cannot be separated from rebuilt-pack evidence. | Mark inherited rows individually and provide the promised source list, or remove the unsupported provenance statement.
- RR-15 | low | length | SKILL.md exceeds roughly 300 lines | Extensive historical settings, software counts and source summaries obscure the actionable workflow. | Move the detailed parameter-frequency table, software census, sampler examples and expanded source annotations to references/parameters.md; retain decision rules and essential safeguards.

## Notes

